id: pm-vcs-legacyreftmp
title: Recover legacy ref publication crash temporaries without hiding legal refs
description: "The former ref writer used destination plus process-id plus .tmp before rename. A crash can leave a complete phantom ref or a truncated ref that conservatively blocks GC. Those names are also legal durable refs, so filename-only automatic skipping or deletion would lose roots. PR 138 prevents new collisions with exclusive .lock temporaries; explicit migration and recovery for existing ambiguous files remains separate."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T20:30:26.002Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T20:32:16.693Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Provide an explicit inspect-first recovery or migration flow with complete and truncated old-writer fixtures; preserve legitimate process-shaped .tmp refs and their reachable objects; never delete or hide ambiguous roots automatically; messages and receipts expose only repository-relative paths.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
